    "instructions": "Charts draw numeric data from the data model. Bind series, slices or values with {\"@path\": \"/sales/series\"} (RFC 6901, leading slash) and send the numbers in updateDataModel; inline literals are for small fixed charts only. Every number is a plain JSON number. Give each chart an explicit height through its modifier and a short label that names what it shows, which screen readers announce. Keep a chart to at most 12 series and 500 points per series; larger data is cut and reported. A value that is not a plain number leaves a gap that the line is drawn through, and a pie slice that is negative or zero is left out. The line and bar actions say that a point or bar was selected, the pie action says only that the chart was tapped, and none says which one.",
    "protocolVersion": "1.0",
    "title": "Charts"
